@metadata
  title: Appeal
  author: Chris Patti
  version: 1.0.0
  story_id: appeal
  description: An interactive adventure celebrating Boston history.

@start DexterGate

:: DexterGate
You are standing outside one of the gates to Harvard University.  A plaque off to the side
tells you that this is Dexter Gate. Always read the plaque! :)

Harvard Square. City Hall is in Central Square, but the beating heart and the living soul
of Cambridge, Massachusetts is right here.

Generations of people have come here to live, work, study, eat, party, or for the more
unfornate find a warm place to huddle against the cold and maybe bum a few bucks for some
food or a bottle off of one of the myriad tourists.

+ [Cross the street to the Harvard Bookstore] -> HarvardBookStore

:: HarvardBookStore

You are a bibliophile. Nothing makes you feel more at home than the very slight musty smell
of old books, well cared for and numerous, loading down the shelves and practically
bursting out of every possible space.

For you, this place is comfort food for the soul.

You aren't looking for anything in particular and you have no target in
mind, you're just dawdling along letting your curiosity be your guide.

A history of Rhodesia (Whew. Bloody and racist. You put that one back
right quick!), an illustrated guide to ducks, and a survivalist's
guide to New England plants later, you settle on a small pile of
books that you put under your arm and decide it's probably time to leave
before you do any more damage to your checkbook... And then...

You feel something tugging at the back of your mind, leading you
to the very back of the store where one book sticks out of the shelf
just slightly.

You scratch your eyes wondering if you need more coffee when you realize
that no, you really ARE seeing the book emanate a faint glow. Well, 
maybe not so much a glow as a slight shimmering in the air around it.

@py
# Grab the book or not
@endpy

